{
  "version": 2,
  "_note": "SOURCING VIABILITY -- a different question from restricted/gated. Gating asks 'will Amazon let me create this listing today?' (getListingsRestrictions answers that). Viability asks 'if I list this freely today, what safety documents will Amazon demand months later, and can I actually produce them?' The electric patio heater was neither gated nor restricted: it listed fine, then Amazon asked for a BS EN 60335-2-30 test report nobody had. As arbitrage/resellers we almost never hold manufacturer safety documentation, so the honest question at sourcing time is whether the obligation is fulfillable at all.",
  "no_match_message": "No document-demand risk detected -- this is NOT a clearance. Amazon can request safety documentation for any product at any time, and detection here is signal-based. Absence of a signal means nothing was recognised, not that nothing will be asked for.",
  "caveat": "Signal-based detection: obvious cases are caught reliably, disguised or vaguely-worded ones may slip through. Treat a hit as a strong prompt to confirm you can obtain the documents BEFORE sourcing, not as a complete list of everything Amazon might ask.",
  "warning_template": "SOURCING RISK [{rule}]: Amazon will likely request {docs}. As a reseller you probably cannot provide these.",
  "matching_note": "Same corroborated-keyword discipline as the restricted checker. 'strong' fires alone. 'corroborating' is a common word (fan, iron, ring, plate, bar, light) that only counts WITH a 'context' word from the same rule -- 'curling iron' fires, 'iron supplement' does not; 'sterling silver ring' fires, 'ring binder' does not. 'exclude' is a hard veto checked first. Accessory adjacency ('patio heater COVER') is applied by listing/restricted.py's shared rule.",
  "doc_note": "Entries matching an id in required_docs.json render that catalogue's name; anything else renders verbatim. Mixing is intentional -- the catalogue stays the one source for shared documents, and product-specific requirements with no catalogue entry are written out in full.",
  "risk_classes": [
